   "fp": "b088980b7e04",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 29,
   "message": "The preset and the review pack disagree on where tokens may be stored. The preset's Tokens rule bans only `localStorage`, but review rule RS7 (plugins/specclaw-review/review-rules/react-spa.md) also flags `sessionStorage` as a major. A build that follows the preset can still be failed by review. Fix: change the preset rule to `no tokens in localStorage or sessionStorage`.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B4",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor",
   "unclassified": false
  },
  {
   "class": "other",
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/presets/react-spa.md",
   "fp": "ca9f4e7f7c6a",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 33,
   "message": "The preset's Links rule bans user-supplied URLs in `href` outright. RS10 in the review pack only requires a scheme check (`javascript:`). The two give different instructions for the same case. Pick one wording and use it in both files, for example `a user-supplied URL in href only after checking its scheme is http(s)`.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B4",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor",
   "unclassified": false
  },
  {
   "class": "other",
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/presets/node.md",
   "fp": "8663a6363428",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 33,
   "message": "The preset's Cors rule says `list explicit origins` (no wildcard at all). ND9 in the review pack flags only a wildcard origin combined with credentials. A wildcard without credentials breaks the preset but passes review. Make the two rules match.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B4",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor",
   "unclassified": false
  },
  {
   "class": "other",
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/tests/run-preset-check-tests.sh",
   "fp": "9b2e5ee24aac",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 154,
   "message": "Two mutant scripts use GNU-only sed syntax: `\\|` alternation in a BRE, and `{h;d}` with no `;` before `}`. On BSD/macOS sed the mutant is not produced as intended and the AC-3 checks fail for the wrong reason. Use two `-e` delete expressions instead of `\\|`, and write `{h;d;}`.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B10",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor",
   "unclassified": false
  }
